  "question": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{FeO}_4^{2-} \\xrightarrow{+2.0 \\mathrm{v}} \\mathrm{Fe}^{3+} \\xrightarrow{0.8 \\mathrm{v}} \\mathrm{Fe}^{2+} \\xrightarrow{-0.5 \\mathrm{v}} \\mathrm{Fe}^0$\nIn the above diagram, the standard electrode potentials are given in volts (over the arrow).\nThe value of $\\mathrm{E}_{\\mathrm{FeO}_4^{2-} / \\mathrm{Fe}^{2+}}^{\\mathrm{O}}$ is"
